*  CN-12 -- NESTED substitution is DEPTH-LIMITED BY DESIGN (top-level only): a
*  keyword member INSIDE an already-substituted tree takes the snapshot-defer road.
*  This pins the reason: full nesting inside an ALT arm crashed m4 while m3 passed
*  (u3 witness, s161-2 -- getenv SEGV via c_rt_dcap_end_ok_open at match end, i.e.
*  arena/stack corruption of the B2 record class; the FINAL graph shape ALT(SPAN,
*  SPAN) is proven fine by its literal twin).  When that emission defect is root-
*  caused, the depth limit deletes and this witness's defer count drops -- output
*  stays exactly this either way.
	&USER_DECLARED_CONSTANTS = 1
	&W2 = SPAN("ab")
	&N2 = SPAN("09")
	&P = &W2 | &N2
	"ab" POS(0) *&P RPOS(0)	:S(Y)F(N)
Y	OUTPUT = "match"	:(END)
N	OUTPUT = "nomatch"
END
